{
 "format": "souls-form-cases/1",
 "about": "eden:drilling_panel and eden:camp_drill_press (from #1860). A panel has nine cells, 1 at the back left to 9 at the front right; a press's cutter has four uses and no refill. Boring a cell (four seconds, a hand free, at the press) leaves a permanent hole and moves one cutter use from the press into the panel, where it stands for the hole's wooden core kept in the rail; a panel holds at most four. Refused: a bored cell ('That cell already has a retained hole/core; choose an unbored cell.'), a spent cutter ('This cutter has exhausted its four coarse boring uses; use another charged press. No refill is offered.'), a full panel ('This panel already retains four holes/cores; choose another unfilled panel.'), full hands ('Put down held objects ...'). The original's cell argument is nine forms (a set whose field comes from an argument is a later format). Handed back: the panel resting on that press, both hands empty, and the press's record of the last panel and worker.",
